{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836932",
      "title": "How (Not) To Connect To A Database",
      "sourceHash": "6e08bfa8de784c8ca19dcd2b4e21519136e5a080bc750451f7947db38f75c22c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "Now, as I already mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 4.32,
          "en": "in the previous lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 9.32,
          "en": "there often are good reasons for having a central server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 14.42,
          "en": "a central backend or database to which multiple instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.58,
          "end": 16.62,
          "en": "of the React app connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.62,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "in order to share data across users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "If you are building an online store, you wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "that different users from different parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "of the world can access the same data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "and can of course also send data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 35.46,
          "en": "can place orders, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.46,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "And you as an owner of the shop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 39.66,
          "en": "of course then also need access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 43.68,
          "en": "to those orders so that you can fulfill them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.68,
          "end": 47.82,
          "en": "Therefore, you often need such a central backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.82,
          "end": 49.47,
          "en": "or database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 52.68,
          "en": "And therefore, an important question is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 57.68,
          "en": "how do you connect your React app to such a database?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.05,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "How can you send data to such a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "and get data out of such a central database?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 70.78999999999999,
          "en": "And the short answer is, you don't, at least not directly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.01,
          "end": 74.13,
          "en": "You don't directly connect your React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.13,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "to a database because if you were to try that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "you would run into security issues.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 83.94,
          "en": "Because what's important to understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.94,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "as a web developer in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "is that when writing code that runs in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 93.6,
          "en": "which is exactly what you're doing with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.6,
          "end": 96.78,
          "en": "all your React application code runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.78,
          "end": 99.6,
          "en": "in the browsers of your visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 101.4,
          "en": "If you are doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 106.4,
          "en": "your visitors can access that code, they can view that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.22,
          "end": 110.03999999999999,
          "en": "And if that code then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.03999999999999,
          "end": 113.75999999999999,
          "en": "contains the credentials to access a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 116.67,
          "en": "your database can get compromised",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.67,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "because users can retrieve those credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 123.15,
          "en": "and access your database to destroy data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 128.15,
          "en": "insert incorrect data, or do all kinds of bad things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 133.05,
          "en": "In addition, you also have certain restrictions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.05,
          "end": 135.12,
          "en": "when writing front-end code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "So code that runs in a browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "For example, you can't easily access a file system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 146.25,
          "en": "Especially not a shared file system that lives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.25,
          "end": 149.88,
          "en": "on some central server or computer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.88,
          "end": 153.723,
          "en": "You don't really have those capabilities in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 158.73,
          "en": "And therefore, instead of directly accessing a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.73,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "or some file system that may hold shared data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.32,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "you instead communicate with a backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 171,
          "en": "which kind of acts as a middleman, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 174.36,
          "en": "So that your front-end React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.36,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "which runs on the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "and where users can theoretically view the entire code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 184.71,
          "en": "that application can reach out to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "So a separate project running on a separate server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 193.8,
          "en": "a computer owned and operated by you, the developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.8,
          "end": 197.25,
          "en": "And it's then on that backend where you can interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 199.14,
          "en": "with databases, et cetera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.14,
          "end": 202.8,
          "en": "because that backend code is inaccessible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 206.46,
          "en": "by the users of your website because only you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.46,
          "end": 209.79,
          "en": "the owner and developer, only you have access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.79,
          "end": 212.643,
          "en": "to the code on such a backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 216.27,
          "en": "And to connect the frontend and the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 216.27,
          "end": 219.27,
          "en": "you use HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 224.07,
          "en": "so that from inside your React application you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.07,
          "end": 229.07,
          "en": "send an HTTP request to the backend to request some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.53,
          "end": 232.35,
          "en": "or to request a change to some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 232.35,
          "end": 236.37,
          "en": "But what's super important, and a safety feature here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 241.37,
          "en": "is that you can only send HTTP requests that are allowed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 241.53,
          "end": 244.53,
          "en": "and accepted by this backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 244.53,
          "end": 247.59,
          "en": "And if a backend doesn't want a certain request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 247.59,
          "end": 248.85,
          "en": "it's not possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.85,
          "end": 252.51,
          "en": "And therefore you can control what users can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 254.37,
          "en": "and can't do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.37,
          "end": 258.27,
          "en": "So to sum it up, if you have a React app that needs to talk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.27,
          "end": 261.06,
          "en": "to a database, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 261.06,
          "end": 264.03,
          "en": "you have to understand that with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 266.16,
          "en": "you are writing client-side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 266.16,
          "end": 269.07,
          "en": "You are building a client-side web application that runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 269.07,
          "end": 271.98,
          "en": "in the browser and where the code can be viewed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.98,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "by the visitors of your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 276.84000000000003,
          "en": "Therefore, you communicate with a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.84000000000003,
          "end": 278.76,
          "en": "through HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.76,
          "end": 282.24,
          "en": "and it's that backend code that then may interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282.24,
          "end": 283.35,
          "en": "with a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.35,
          "end": 287.67,
          "en": "because that code is not exposed to your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.67,
          "end": 290.13,
          "en": "Instead, you control which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.13,
          "end": 293.22,
          "en": "of requests should be possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.22,
          "end": 298.22,
          "en": "by exposing so-called endpoints on your backend API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.92,
          "end": 302.763,
          "en": "Simply, URLs that accept certain requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.81,
          "end": 305.82,
          "en": "You should never try to connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.82,
          "end": 309.27,
          "en": "to a database directly from inside your React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 309.27,
          "end": 313.62,
          "en": "because you would expose your database credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 313.62,
          "end": 317.34,
          "en": "And therefore it's quite common to have separate frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.34,
          "end": 319.14,
          "en": "and backend projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 319.14,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "where you also don't have to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.33,
          "en": "the same programming language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.33,
          "end": 325.8,
          "en": "When building a React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.8,
          "end": 328.05,
          "en": "you are of course using JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 328.05,
          "end": 329.82,
          "en": "but you could build your backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.82,
          "end": 333.403,
          "en": "with any language that can be used for that like PHP,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 333.403,
          "end": 338.253,
          "en": "C#, or also JavaScript with NodeJS, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 342.99,
          "en": "You can also build full-stack React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 342.99,
          "end": 346.95,
          "en": "where you kind of blend frontend and backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 346.95,
          "end": 350.34000000000003,
          "en": "whilst still ensuring that the backend code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 350.34000000000003,
          "end": 353.90999999999997,
          "en": "can't be accessed with extra frameworks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 353.90999999999997,
          "end": 357.27,
          "en": "and libraries like NextJS or Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 357.27,
          "end": 358.8,
          "en": "And later in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 358.8,
          "end": 362.94,
          "en": "I do indeed have a thorough introduction to NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 362.94,
          "end": 365.43,
          "en": "which gives you a slightly different approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 365.43,
          "end": 369.18,
          "en": "for building such backend-powered web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 369.18,
          "end": 370.86,
          "en": "with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 370.86,
          "end": 373.14,
          "en": "But in this section, we'll take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 373.14,
          "end": 374.76,
          "en": "at how you can connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 374.76,
          "end": 378.39300000000003,
          "en": "to a standalone backend from inside your React app.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}